window.docContents[174].resolve({"/External-Kernels/#Lean-__________________--____________--Lean-____________--______--_________":{"contents":"官方 Lean 内核使用无字段的构造器 Lean.Declaration.quotDecl 作为输入来声明商类型相关声明。\n随后，它会将组成商类型包的四个声明加入环境。\n为方便使用，导出格式包含这些生成声明的数据。\n\n{\n  \"quot\": {\n    \"name\": NameIdx,\n    \"levelParams\": Array<NameIdx>,\n    \"type\": ExprIdx,\n    \"kind\": \"type\" | \"ctor\" | \"lift\" | \"ind\"\n  }\n}\n\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009外部内核\u0009Lean 导出格式\u0009声明","header":"27.1.5.5. 商类型","id":"/External-Kernels/#Lean-__________________--____________--Lean-____________--______--_________"},"/IO/Async/#Lean-__________________--IO--____________--______-I___O--______--UDP":{"contents":"与 TCP 不同，UDP 无连接：单个套接字无需先建立连接，就能与任意地址收发称为数据报的独立消息。\nUDP 不提供确保数据报实际到达的机制；这需要由应用层处理。\n数据报还可以通过广播或组播同时投递给多个接收方。\n\n创建新的 UDP 套接字。\n\n将 UDP 套接字绑定到给定地址。\n启用地址复用，以允许重新绑定同一地址。\n\n将 UDP 套接字与给定地址和端口关联，使通过该套接字发送的每条消息都自动发送到该目的地。\n\n通过 UDP 套接字发送数据。\naddr 参数指定目的地址。\n若 addr 为 none，则将数据发送到通过 connect 设置的默认对端地址。\n\n通过 UDP 套接字发送多个数据缓冲区。\naddr 参数指定目的地址。\n若 addr 为 none，则将数据发送到通过 connect 设置的默认对端地址。\n\n从 UDP 套接字接收数据。\nsize 是要接收的最大字节数。\n当有数据可用或发生错误时，承诺就绪。\n如果此前未使用 bind 绑定套接字，则自动将其绑定到 0.0.0.0（所有接口）及随机端口。\n此外，不支持与 recvSelector 并行调用此函数。大于 size 的数据报会被整体丢弃，并抛出 IO.Error.resourceExhausted，而不是返回被截断的前缀。\n套接字仍可使用，因此接收循环应对每个数据报分别捕获该错误。\n\n获取 UDP 套接字的本地地址。\n\n获取 UDP 套接字的远端地址。\n对未连接的句柄，会抛出 .invalidArgument 错误。\n\n启用或禁用 UDP 套接字的广播。\n\n设置出站数据包的生存时间（TTL）。\n\n启用或禁用 UDP 套接字的多播回环。\n\n设置多播数据包的生存时间（TTL）。\n\n设置发送数据包的多播接口。\n\n设置加入或离开多播组的成员关系。\n\n多播操作的成员关系类型。\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009IO\u0009异步编程\u0009异步 I/O\u0009网络","header":"22.12.7.1.2. UDP","id":"/IO/Async/#Lean-__________________--IO--____________--______-I___O--______--UDP"},"/Source Files and Modules/#Lean-__________________--__________________--Module-System-Errors-and-Patterns":{"contents":"The following list contains common errors one might encounter when using the module system and especially porting existing files to the module system:Unknown constant errors\n\nCheck whether a private definition is being accessed in the public scope.\nIf so, the problem can be solved by making the current declaration private as well, or by placing the reference into the private scope using the private modifier on a field or by for a proof.\n\nDefinitional equality errors, especially after porting\n\nFailures of expected definitional equalities are usually due to a missing expose attribute on a definition or alternatively, if imported, an import all.\nPrefer the former if anyone outside your library might feasibly require the same access.\nThe error message should list non-exposed definitions that could not be unfolded.\nThis may also appear as a kernel error when a tactic directly emits proof terms that reference specific declarations without going through the elaborator, such as for proof by reflection.\nIn this case, there is no readily available trace for debugging; consider using @[expose]‍ sections generously on the closure of relevant modules.\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009源文件与模块","header":"5.6. Module System Errors and Patterns","id":"/Source Files and Modules/#Lean-__________________--__________________--Module-System-Errors-and-Patterns"}});